{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 110,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is sponsored by the YouTube Red\nSci-Fi Series \"Lifeline\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4920,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For ages I’ve been wanting to make a video\nanalyzing time travel in fiction – not the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9200,
    "dDurationMs": 4719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magical or physical mechanisms by which the\ntime travel is supposedly achieved , but rather,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13919,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the different ways time travel can influence\ncausality (and thus the plot) within the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18680,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of each story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19860,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Needless to say, there are spoilers ahead!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22270,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's start with Ender's Game by Orson Scott\nCard – time travel in this book is actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26920,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "100% realistic: the characters experience\nslower passage of time when they travel close"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31390,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to light speed, allowing just a few days or\nmonths to pass for those traveling while years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36160,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pass on earth or other planets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38550,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's traveling forward through time like we\nnormally do, but at different rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43030,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This kind of time travel doesn't \"change the\npast\" or allow characters to make different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47190,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decisions than the ones they already did – it's\nall one consistent historical trajectory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52170,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The original Planet of the Apes film is similar,\nwhere astronauts experience extreme time dilation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57220,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then crash land on a strange ape-ruled\nplanet that (major spoiler) turns out to just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62920,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be earth in the distant future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65000,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what about actual time-travel time travel?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66990,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I would say there are two big distinguishing\nfeatures between different types of time travel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71530,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72530,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is whether or not the time traveler\nis there when history happens the \"first time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76350,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around\" – that is, is there a kind of \"self-consistency\"\nwhere, since time travel takes you to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81170,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "past, when the past happened the first time,\nthe time-traveling version of you was always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85650,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there to begin with?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86750,
    "dDurationMs": 4189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or does the very act of time traveling to\nthe past change what happened and force the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90939,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe onto a different trajectory of history\nfrom the one you experienced prior to traveling?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95700,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the second distinguishing feature is:\nwho has free will when somebody is time traveling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99780,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, whose actions are allowed to move history\nonto a different trajectory, and whose aren't?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104240,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the simplest time travels is \"do-over\"\ntime travel, where you essentially get to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "re-play history starting exactly as it was\nat a certain point, with the only caveat being"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you remember your experiences from already\nhaving tried various possible future timelines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(while no one else does)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s essentially like playing a video game\nwhere you can start a level over with the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111900,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foresight of what you did wrong the first\ntime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113540,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in Groundhog Day Bill Murray's\ncharacter relives the same day over and over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118369,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again, and though he can make different choices\neach time, he always starts back at the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122820,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point (except with new memories of his previous\nchoices)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126210,
    "dDurationMs": 4659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, until he figures out the one exact\nset of choices that frees him from the loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130869,
    "dDurationMs": 5061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I consider \"A Christmas Carol\" to be in this\nvein, too, even though it may not seem like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135930,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time travel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136930,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because Scrooge gets to visit the future\nof his current timeline, even though he has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140410,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no ability to affect the timeline directly\nwhile \"visiting\", he can still change his"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145040,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actions in the present based on what he learns,\nessentially getting a “do-over.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148580,
    "dDurationMs": 5730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The video game Braid is built on the idea\nof “do-overs”, where you get to rewind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154310,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few seconds and try something different\n(though there are some things that are immune"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157610,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to going back in time and don't \"rewind\",\nwhich is what makes the game interesting)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161489,
    "dDurationMs": 4181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Braid also has another kind of time travel,\nwhere you go back to your past as a separate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165670,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "individual, and the past version of you is\nthere with no free will, just doing exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170440,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what you did the first time around, while\n\"time-traveling you\" can change the course"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174670,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175670,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also how the video \"Clock Blockers\"\nby the Corridor Digital youtube channel works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179810,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then there's time travel where the very\nact of going to the past or future creates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184250,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a fully new trajectory of history because\ntime-traveling you weren't there the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188680,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time around, and now you are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190710,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This includes the typical \"anything goes\"\ntime travel movies like Bill \u0026 Ted's Excellent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194970,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Adventure, Back to the Future, Star Trek First\nContact, and so on, where you can kind of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199470,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instantly jump back and forth to any point\nin time you want, potentially resulting in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203530,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multiple versions of yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205340,
    "dDurationMs": 3490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a causality perspective, anything you\ndo in the past (and even just the act of going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208830,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back in time) redirects the course of history\nonto a new timeline – in Back to the Future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213580,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Marty's interference with his parents falling\nin love results in the timeline of history"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217500,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being redirected towards a version of the\nfuture where he doesn't exist and so he starts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221630,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to disappear from photos and real life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223890,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even after correcting that major deviation,\nhis interactions with his parents while he’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228300,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the past result in them being very different\npeople when he returns to his present time;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232500,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he accidentally caused history to progress\nin a slightly different direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236650,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The movie ”Looper\" is similar, but there's\na little more circularity because when you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240450,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jump to the past, you cause history to branch\nonto on a trajectory where, in the future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245330,
    "dDurationMs": 3129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the younger you also goes back in time the\nsame way you just did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248459,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both you and your past self still have enough\nfree will to change that forward course of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252489,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "history, though, which results in weirdness\nlike you getting new memories when your past"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256479,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "self does things you yourself didn't do, or\nif they lose a body part, suddenly you'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261069,
    "dDurationMs": 3871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lose it too, replaced by an old scar on your\nown body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264940,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, changes to the present affect not just\nfuture timelines, but also future timelines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269210,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that wrap back around to the present!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271629,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The indie film Primer is in the same vein,\nexcept that it takes the plot device of time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276229,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travel to the extreme, with time travel within\ntime travel within time travel, time-traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281909,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "characters interacting with other time-traveling\nversions of themselves, bringing time machines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285699,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with them to the past inside other time machines,\nand so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289370,
    "dDurationMs": 4639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But beyond the complexity, there are two things\nthat make Primer stand out: first, time travel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294009,
    "dDurationMs": 5411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the past isn't an instantaneous jump, but\nactually takes time: to go back 6 hours, you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299420,
    "dDurationMs": 3459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sit in the time machine for what feels like\n6 hours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302879,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And time travel can't take you back to a time\nbefore a given time machine was initially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307229,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "activated, since of course, the machine can\nonly be taking you back in time inside it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311369,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if it's turned on, so the first time it was\nturned on is the farthest back in time you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315379,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316919,
    "dDurationMs": 1511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a nice logic to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318430,
    "dDurationMs": 5109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which brings us to perhaps my all time favorite\nof all fictional time travel: Harry Potter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323539,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Prisoner of Azkaban."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324639,
    "dDurationMs": 5971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's an \"instantly jump back in time\" kind\nof time travel that doesn't actually generate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330610,
    "dDurationMs": 1359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any new timelines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331969,
    "dDurationMs": 4461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It manages that because in this universe,\nwhile you were experiencing your initial,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336430,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pre-time-travel passage through a particular\npoint in history, your \"time-traveling clone\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340219,
    "dDurationMs": 4621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was also already there, doing everything you’ll\neventually do when you time travel yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344840,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, Harry and friends are saved from\ndying by their time-traveling selves, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349550,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first time through that timeline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351460,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It makes so much sense – if you go back\nin time, you really and truly were present"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356340,
    "dDurationMs": 2909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at that point in time all along!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359249,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This also means that during the period of\noverlap, the time-traveling you has no actual"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363759,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free will, since everything you do has in\nsome sense already been done, which Harry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367839,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comprehends when he realizes he has to save\nhis past self because he was already saved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372949,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by his future self when he was in the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375659,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think I love this kind of time travel because\nit manages to be logically consistent: it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380090,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time travel to the past where you can't change\nthe past, because the past already happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384830,
    "dDurationMs": 5039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's only one timeline – the one\nin which time travelers arrive from the future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389869,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do stuff, and at some later date, leave to\ngo to the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393729,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Logical consistency is a primary thing that,\nyou may have noticed, I think lays the foundation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398469,
    "dDurationMs": 5170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for good time travel stories – not because\nlogical consistency is important in an of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403639,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "itself, but because, most of the time, in\norder to care about the characters in a story,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407689,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have to believe that actions have consequences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410009,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If everything is just a meaningless series\nof events, then we almost don't have a story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414710,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's really helpful if there are rules\nby which the universe of the story functions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419270,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatever those rules may be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423709,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Speaking of actions with consequences, I finally\ngot the kick in the pants I needed to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428319,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video from my friends at the Corridor\nDigital YouTube channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431699,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They've asked me to help promote their new\nYouTube Red Original Series, \"Lifeline”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435490,
    "dDurationMs": 4799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which, minor spoilers ahead... is a sci fi\naction thriller with time travel in it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440289,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What kind of time travel, you ask?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442259,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, if somebody dies in the future,\nthat sends a message back to the present,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446610,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which allows people to jump forward to just\nbefore the time the person dies and change"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451069,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the trajectory of history from that point\nonwards, averting their death."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454919,
    "dDurationMs": 2661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as you might imagine, things eventually\ngo awry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457580,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, you can check out the first episode\nof Lifeline for free on the Corridor Digital"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461899,
    "dDurationMs": 4461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "channel or by following the links onscreen\nor in the description . And fun facts: I actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466360,
    "dDurationMs": 5299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know the Corridor guys from back before MinutePhysics,\nwhen I was doing special effects for the \"freddiew\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471659,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472659,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We also all grew up in neighboring towns in\nMinnesota and even competed against each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477119,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in high school sports , though we didn't know\neach other at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480249,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But enough trivia – go check out their\nshow!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
